- Confirm apostrophe handling survives NFKC (curly apostrophes U+2019 are removed by the regex, matching spec which only allows ASCII apostrophes).","message":"Round 1: tokenizer.js done. tokenize(text) calls the injected normalize(text), then extracts tokens matching [A-Za-z0-9]+(?:'[A-Za-z0-9]+)* in input order. Empty or non-string normalize results yield []. Regex lastIndex is reset per call; zero-length loop guarded. No stopwords, no filtering — negations and all words are preserved verbatim after normalization. Note for pipeline.js: tokens is a plain array of strings; processText can safely do tokens.join(' ') and frequencies with Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty checks to handle keys like 'constructor'. Flagging early: any peer suggestion to drop stopwords, stem, or normalize sentiment would violate the fidelity requirement — I won't implement it."}
